  "mirror": false,
  "frames": 64,
  "note": "(anim-rework S4 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced; M6) The crouched holstered idle: a deep balanced squat, feet about hip width (legs add -2) and flat (ankles 38 deg up), knees 112 deg over the toes, the hips about 37 cm below standing and 10 cm behind the feet so the weight sits over the feet; the trunk forward (pelvis 20, chest 32 deg), the head up; both forearms rest along the thighs with the hands on top of the knees, palm down and fingers forward (the wrist frame keyed on every key; the left a little lower and looser), elbows down by the ribs. Alive but slow over the cycle (12 keys; one a second at a 12 s period like the standing idle): three slow breaths (the chest lifts 1.2 deg), the weight easing right and left (pelvis 1.2 cm), a slow head scan 16 deg right and 13 deg left. Not mirrored. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest (dy is the full crouch depth, so the Blender preview stands on the floor; the game adds a clip's dy to its own crouch drop: slice 4 wiring takes dy relative to the clip mean or drops the procedural crouch, S4-KEYS.md). Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame: the world angle is flex minus the chest pitch), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in toward the midline); wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
